  <layout>One page of verse; running head at top; a marginal note at the lower right ("Maistrisee") set beside the last line.</layout>
  <page_number />
  <running_head>THEOD. BEZÆ</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" para="true">Priere de l'ame fidelle, se trouuant lassée</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="1">és trauaux de son pelerinage.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">HElas mon Dieu, quand sera-</l>
    <l n="4">ce Que ie pourray voir ta face?</l>
    <l n="5">Quand ce throne glorieux</l>
    <l n="6">Sera-il ueu de mes yeux?</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Face non pas courroucée,</l>
    <l n="8">Mais en celuy appaisée,</l>
    <l n="9">Qui m'a d'en tout endebté</l>
    <l n="10">Faict en du tout acquitté.</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Throne aux meschans effroyable,</l>
    <l n="12">Comme aux tiens tresdesirable,</l>
    <l n="13">Que tu as faits, d'ennemis,</l>
    <l n="14">Par toy mesmes, tes amis.</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Las quand la chair qui me tue,</l>
    <l n="16">Par ton esprit abbatue,</l>
    <l n="17">Pour n'en releuer iamais,</l>
    <l n="18">Me laissera elle en paix?</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Quand prendra fin ceste guerre</l>
    <l n="20">Entre mon ciel &amp; ma Terre?</l>
    <l n="21">Quand ne debattront en moy</l>
    <l n="22">La defiance &amp; la foy?</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Las quand la Volonté miene</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="Las quand la" line_from="23" line_to="23">Maistrisee</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>Marginal note at lower right reads "Maistrisee", beside the final line. Some letters in the scan are doubtful, notably in "Sera-il Veu", "Faict Dieu" and "Iamais", which were read as printed where legible. The first word of the first stanza is a large initial H.</notes>
</page>
